proof.text:
For $F,G\in\mathcal C$, expand $a_{F,G}$ and use the symmetry compatibility of the lax functor $R$ in [def-sfb-finite-lower-star-lax-monoidal], followed by naturality of the symmetry for $\eta_F$ and $\eta_G$:
$$\begin{aligned}
R(\beta^{\mathcal D}_{LF,LG})\circ a_{F,G}
&=m_{LG,LF}\circ\beta^{\mathcal C}_{RLF,RLG}\circ(\eta_F\otimes\eta_G)\\
&=m_{LG,LF}\circ(\eta_G\otimes\eta_F)\circ\beta^{\mathcal C}_{F,G}
=a_{G,F}\circ\beta^{\mathcal C}_{F,G}.
\end{aligned}$$
All these maps have source $F\otimes G$ and target $R(LG\otimes LF)$; the two equalities are respectively the defining braided-functor equation for $R$ and the defining naturality square of $\beta^{\mathcal C}$.
